22A1</text><sources><source name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>TARI ISAO ET. AL.: 'Synthesis of Halogenated Esters of Flurinaterd Carboxylic Acids by the Regio- and Stereospecific Addition of Acyl Hypochlorites to Olefins' J. ORG. CHEM. vol. 45, no. 7, 1980, pages 1214 - 1217, XP002929014</text> <sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources> </nplcit> </non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASAHI GLASS CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MUROFUSHI HIDENOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAZOE TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TATEMASU SHIN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAHI GLASS COMPANY, LIMITED</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MUROFUSHI, HIDENOBU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAZOE, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TATEMASU, SHIN</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, KUNIO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MUROFUSHI HIDENOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKAZOE TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TATEMASU SHIN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MUROFUSHI, HIDENOBU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKAZOE, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TATEMASU, SHIN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, KUNIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for producing a fluorine compound from inexpensive materials.  The process comprises reacting a compound (I), e.g., R&lt;A&gt;CH2OH, with a compound (II), e.g., XCOR&lt;B&gt;, to form a compound (III), e.g., R&lt;A&gt;CH2OCOR&lt;B&gt;, fluorinating the compound (III) in a liquid phase to form a compound (IV), e.g., R&lt;AF&gt;CF2OCOR&lt;BF&gt;, and converting the compound (IV) into a compound (V), e.g., R&lt;AF&gt;COF, and/or a compound (VI), e.g., R&lt;BF&gt;COF.  R&lt;A&gt; is alkyl, etc.; R&lt;B&gt; is perhalogenoalkyl, etc.; R&lt;AF&gt; and R&lt;BF&gt; are fluorinated R&lt;A&gt; and R&lt;B&gt;, respectively; and X is a halogen.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de production d'un composé de fluor à partir de matières peu onéreuses. Ce procédé consiste à faire réagir un composé (I), par exemple R&lt;A&gt;CH2OH, avec un composé (II), par exemple, XCOR&lt;B&gt;, afin d'obtenir un composé (III), par exemple, R&lt;A&gt;CH2OCOR&lt;B&gt;, à fluorer ce composé (IV), par exemple, R&lt;AF&gt;CF2OCOR&lt;BF&gt;, et à convertir ce composé (IV) en un composé (V), par exemple, R&lt;AF&gt;COF et/ou en un composé (VI), par exemple, R&lt;BF&gt;COF. R&lt;A&gt; représente alkyle, etc. ; R&lt;B&gt; représente perhalogénoalkyle, etc. ; R&lt;AF&gt; et R&lt;BF&gt; représentent, respectivement, R&lt;A&gt; et R&lt;B&gt; fluorés ; et x représente halogène.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>